.SS "enum \fBlibusb_option\fP"

.PP
Available option values for \fBlibusb_set_option()\fP and \fBlibusb_init_context()\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\f(BILIBUSB_OPTION_LOG_LEVEL \fP
Set the log message verbosity\&. This option must be provided an argument of type \fBlibusb_log_level\fP\&. The default level is LIBUSB_LOG_LEVEL_NONE, which means no messages are ever printed\&. If you choose to increase the message verbosity level, ensure that your application does not close the stderr file descriptor\&.

.PP
You are advised to use level LIBUSB_LOG_LEVEL_WARNING\&. libusb is conservative with its message logging and most of the time, will only log messages that explain error conditions and other oddities\&. This will help you debug your software\&.

.PP
If the LIBUSB_DEBUG environment variable was set when libusb was initialized, this option does nothing: the message verbosity is fixed to the value in the environment variable\&.

.PP
If libusb was compiled without any message logging, this option does nothing: you'll never get any messages\&.

.PP
If libusb was compiled with verbose debug message logging, this option does nothing: you'll always get messages from all levels\&. 
.TP
\f(BILIBUSB_OPTION_USE_USBDK \fP
Use the UsbDk backend for a specific context, if available\&. This option should be set at initialization with \fBlibusb_init_context()\fP otherwise unspecified behavior may occur\&.

.PP
Only valid on Windows\&. Ignored on all other platforms\&. 
.TP
\f(BILIBUSB_OPTION_NO_DEVICE_DISCOVERY \fP
Do not scan for devices\&. With this option set, libusb will skip scanning devices in \fBlibusb_init_context()\fP\&.

.PP
Hotplug functionality will also be deactivated\&.

.PP
The option is useful in combination with \fBlibusb_wrap_sys_device()\fP, which can access a device directly without prior device scanning\&.

.PP
This is typically needed on Android, where access to USB devices is limited\&.

.PP
This option should only be used with \fBlibusb_init_context()\fP otherwise unspecified behavior may occur\&.

.PP
Only valid on Linux\&. Ignored on all other platforms\&. 
.TP
\f(BILIBUSB_OPTION_LOG_CB \fP
Set the context log callback function\&. Set the log callback function either on a context or globally\&. This option must be provided an argument of type \fBlibusb_log_cb\fP\&. Using this option with a NULL context is equivalent to calling \fBlibusb_set_log_cb()\fP with mode \fBLIBUSB_LOG_CB_GLOBAL\fP\&. Using it with a non-NULL context is equivalent to calling \fBlibusb_set_log_cb()\fP with mode \fBLIBUSB_LOG_CB_CONTEXT\fP\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void libusb_set_debug (\fBlibusb_context\fP * ctx, int level)"

.PP
Deprecated\&. Use \fBlibusb_set_option()\fP or \fBlibusb_init_context()\fP instead, with the \fBLIBUSB_OPTION_LOG_LEVEL\fP option\&. 
.SS "void libusb_set_log_cb (\fBlibusb_context\fP * ctx, \fBlibusb_log_cb\fP cb, int mode)"

.PP
Set log handler\&. libusb will redirect its log messages to the provided callback function\&. libusb supports redirection of per context and global log messages\&. Log messages sent to the context will be sent to the global log handler too\&.

.PP
If libusb is compiled without message logging or USE_SYSTEM_LOGGING_FACILITY is defined then global callback function will never be called\&. If ENABLE_DEBUG_LOGGING is defined then per context callback function will never be called\&.

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.23, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x01000107

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIctx\fP context on which to assign log handler, or NULL for the default context\&. Parameter ignored if only LIBUSB_LOG_CB_GLOBAL mode is requested\&. 
.br
\fIcb\fP pointer to the callback function, or NULL to stop log messages redirection 
.br
\fImode\fP mode of callback function operation\&. Several modes can be selected for a single callback function, see \fBlibusb_log_cb_mode\fP for a description\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlibusb_log_cb\fP, \fBlibusb_log_cb_mode\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int API_EXPORTEDV libusb_set_option (\fBlibusb_context\fP * ctx, enum \fBlibusb_option\fP option,  \&.\&.\&.)"

.PP
Set an option in the library\&. Use this function to configure a specific option within the library\&.

.PP
Some options require one or more arguments to be provided\&. Consult each option's documentation for specific requirements\&.

.PP
If the context ctx is NULL, the option will be added to a list of default options that will be applied to all subsequently created contexts\&.

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.22, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x01000106

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIctx\fP context on which to operate 
.br
\fIoption\fP which option to set 
.br
\fI\&.\&.\&.\fP any required arguments for the specified option
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fBLIBUSB_SUCCESS\fP on success 

.PP
\fBLIBUSB_ERROR_INVALID_PARAM\fP if the option or arguments are invalid 

.PP
\fBLIBUSB_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\fP if the option is valid but not supported on this platform 

.PP
\fBLIBUSB_ERROR_NOT_FOUND\fP if LIBUSB_OPTION_USE_USBDK is valid on this platform but UsbDk is not available 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int libusb_init (\fBlibusb_context\fP ** ctx)"

.PP
Deprecated initialization function\&. Equivalent to calling libusb_init_context with no options\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlibusb_init_context\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int libusb_init_context (\fBlibusb_context\fP ** ctx, const struct \fBlibusb_init_option\fP options[], int num_options)"

.PP
Initialize libusb\&. This function must be called before calling any other libusb function\&.

.PP
If you do not provide an output location for a context pointer, a default context will be created\&. If there was already a default context, it will be reused (and nothing will be initialized/reinitialized and options will be ignored)\&. If num_options is 0 then options is ignored and may be NULL\&.

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.27, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x0100010A

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIctx\fP Optional output location for context pointer\&. Only valid on return code 0\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP Optional array of options to set on the new context\&. 
.br
\fInum_options\fP Number of elements in the options array\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
0 on success, or a LIBUSB_ERROR code on failure 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
libusb_contexts 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void libusb_exit (\fBlibusb_context\fP * ctx)"

.PP
Deinitialize libusb\&. Should be called after closing all open devices and before your application terminates\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIctx\fP the context to deinitialize, or NULL for the default context 
.RE
.PP

